# The catch-up raises a tree-wide floor instead of its own initiator's (#5697
# review, S2; per-initiator routing floors). Shard root s2 has already caught up
# and is live at its own floor plus one. L's shard root then catches up over a
# predating marker whose generation is higher, and raises the floor for every
# initiator. s2's live generation is now at or below its floor, and the WAL
# refuses every claim it makes. Moved from the design's
# LiveGenerationAboveFloorCatchUpTreeWide.
MODULE: LiveGenerationAboveFloorCatchUpTreeWide
TARGET: LiveGenerationAboveFloor
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a catch-up over one shard root's predating marker raises every initiator's routing floor
PERTURBS: CatchUp

--- FIND
        /\ rowFloor' = [rowFloor EXCEPT !["s"] = rc]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the floor is raised tree-wide.
        /\ rowFloor' = [i \in Inits |-> IF i = "s" THEN rc ELSE Max2(rowFloor[i], rc)]
--- END
